/T1_2 9.75 Tf
0.1335 Tc 0 Tw -45 -24 Td
(8.6.1.3)Tj
0.1373 Tc 0.1522 Tw 45 0 Td
(End of Data \(EOD\)\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1428 Tc -0.1622 Tw 93.75 0 Td
(End of Data is used to signal the end of transmission by the originator \of a frame. )Tj
0.1125 Tc 1.0676 Tw -93.75 -24 Td
(The In-Frame Response \(IFR\) section of the frame, if used, begins imme\diately after the EOD bit \(see)Tj
0.1137 Tc 0.1758 Tw 0 -12 TD
(Figure 11\).  If the In-Frame Response feature is not used, then the bus\ would remain in the passive state)Tj
0.0687 Tc 0.1526 Tw T*
(for an additional bit time, thereby signifying an End of Frame \(EOF\).)Tj
0.1097 Tc -0.0545 Tw 0 -24 TD
(For In-Frame Response, the response byte\(s\) are driven by the responde\rs and begin with the rising edge)Tj
0.0695 Tc 0.1177 Tw 0 -12 TD
(of the first bit of the response, Tp4 after the rising edge of the last \bit sent from the originator of the frame.)Tj
0.1246 Tc -0.3351 Tw 0 -24 TD
(If the first bit of the response byte does not occur at Tp4, and the bus\ remains passive for one additional bit)Tj
0.0962 Tc 0.105 Tw 0 -12 TD
(time \(total time Tp5\) then the originator and all receivers must consi\der the frame complete \(i.e., EOD has)Tj
0.0476 Tc 0.2419 Tw T*
(been transformed into an EOF\).)Tj
0.2523 Tc -0.5253 Tw 129 -168 Td
(FIGURE 11\227END OF DATA SYMBOL)Tj
0.1329 Tc 0 Tw -129 -24 Td
(NOTE\227)Tj
0.0869 Tc 0.1193 Tw (Last bit of a frame may be the last data bit, last CRC bit, or last In-F\rame Response bit.)Tj
/T1_2 9.75 Tf
0.1335 Tc 0 Tw -45 -24 Td
(8.6.1.4)Tj
0.051 Tc 0.2385 Tw 45 0 Td
(End of Frame \(EOF\)\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1059 Tc 0.0836 Tw 100.5 0 Td
(The completion of the EOF defines the end of a frame \(by definition, an\ EOD forms)Tj
0.1083 Tc 0.9312 Tw -100.5 -12 Td
(the first part of the EOF\227see Figure 13\).  After the last transmissi\on byte \(including in-frame response)Tj
0.083 Tc -0.0935 Tw T*
(bytes where applicable\), the bus will be left in a passive state.  When\ EOF has expired \(Tp5 after the rising)Tj
0.1022 Tc -0.0855 Tw T*
(edge of the last bit\), all receivers will consider the transmission com\plete.)Tj
