0.0931 Tc 1.1606 Tw 183.75 0 Td
(The data bus can be in one of two valid states  active or passive.)Tj
0.1023 Tc 0.5622 Tw -183.75 -12 Td
(For clarity in the following sections, a rising edge is a transition fro\m the passive to active state and a falling)Tj
0.1395 Tc -0.3 Tw T*
(edge is a transition from the active to the passive state.)Tj
0.1272 Tc 2.1123 Tw 0 -24 TD
(There are two methods of bit encoding specified in this document, Pulse \Width Modulation \(PWM\) and)Tj
0.1038 Tc 0.5857 Tw 0 -12 TD
(Variable Pulse Width \(VPW\) modulation.  The timing diagrams that follo\w represent the requirements for the)Tj
0.098 Tc -0.1367 Tw T*
(logical waveform.  It is the transmitter's responsibility to transmit bi\ts/symbols which are valid \(i.e., meets these)Tj
0.0998 Tc 0.9397 Tw T*
(specifications\).  In some contention situations, the transmitter will h\ave to re-synchronize to ensure that the)Tj
0.1035 Tc 0.3266 Tw T*
(falling edge is within specification.  The requirements associated with \the reception of these bits and symbols)Tj
0.072 Tc 0.1292 Tw T*
(are not stated explicitly in this specification, but are to be derived f\rom transmitter specifications by the module)Tj
0.1118 Tc 1.011 Tw T*
(or circuit designer.  It is expected that the receiver will employ a sim\ple clock-driven digital filter and digital)Tj
0.1156 Tc 1.6203 Tw T*
(integrator or majority vote sampling circuit for decoding data and maint\aining \223clock\224 synchronization.  All)Tj
0.0929 Tc -0.0534 Tw T*
(timing requirements are specified in Section 9.)Tj
0.1462 Tc -0.19 Tw 0 -24 TD
