0.0499 Tc 0.2396 Tw ( \(IFR\)\227)Tj
0.1116 Tc 5.4279 Tw (For In-Frame Response, the response byte\(s\) are transmitted by the)Tj
0.1164 Tc -0.2912 Tw -73.5 -12 Td
(responders and begin after EOD.  If the first bit of the in-frame respon\se byte does not occur at this point and)Tj
0.1051 Tc 1.3928 Tw T*
(the bus remains passive for a period of time defined as EOF, then the or\iginator and all receivers must)Tj
0.1327 Tc 0.1568 Tw T*
(consider the frame complete.  In-frame response bytes may take one of th\e following forms \(refer to Figure)Tj
0.2072 Tc 0 Tw T*
(5\):)Tj
-0.3158 Tc 0 -24 TD
(a.)Tj
-0.0131 Tc 18 0 Td
(None)Tj
-0.3158 Tc -18 -12 Td
(b.)Tj
0.1075 Tc -0.0323 Tw 18 0 Td
(A single byte transmitted from a single recipient, typically a unique id\entifier \(ID\) or address.)Tj
-0.4178 Tc 0 Tw -18 -12 Td
(c.)Tj
0.1158 Tc 0.2206 Tw 18 0 Td
(Multiple bytes, a single byte transmitted from each recipient.  The effe\ct is to concatenate the individual)Tj
0.1105 Tc 1.779 Tw 0 -12 TD
(response bytes into a response \223stream.\224  The response byte from e\ach recipient must be unique,)Tj
0.0932 Tc 1.0869 Tw T*
(typically a physical address \(ID n\).  Arbitration takes place during t\he response process so that each)Tj
0.1113 Tc 0.7407 Tw T*
(recipient, if arbitration is lost during its response byte, will retrans\mit the single byte until the recipient)Tj
0.0897 Tc 1.8873 Tw T*
(observes its unique byte in the response stream.  Once a given recipient\ observes its own unique)Tj
0.1063 Tc 0.7601 Tw T*
(response byte, it discontinues the transmission process to allow any rem\aining responders to transmit)Tj
0.1148 Tc -0.5753 Tw T*
(their byte. )Tj
-0.3158 Tc 0 Tw -18 -12 Td
(d.)Tj
0.1256 Tc 0.2764 Tw 18 0 Td
(One or more data bytes, all from a single recipient.  A CRC byte may be \appended to the data byte\(s\).)Tj
0.1379 Tc 0.3884 Tw T*
(The CRC byte is calculated as described in 7.4.1, except only the data i\n the response is used for the)Tj
0.0908 Tc -0.5513 Tw T*
(CRC calculation.)Tj
0.1114 Tc 1.1928 Tw -18 -20.25 Td
(Refer to SAE J2178/1 for a detailed discussion of the different IFR type\s and for determination of which)Tj
0.0933 Tc 0.1962 Tw T*
(message types utilize which IFR types.)Tj
0.0917 Tc 0.1978 Tw 0 -24 TD
(If in-frame response bytes are used, the overall frame/message length li\mit remains in effect.  The sum total)Tj
0.1016 Tc -0.1038 Tw 0 -12 TD
(of data bytes, CRC bytes, and in-frame response bytes shall not exceed t\he frame length as specified in 9.2.)Tj
