(Arbitration\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1254 Tc 0.3372 Tw (The process of resolving which frame, or In-Frame Response data, continu\es to be transmitted)Tj
0.1546 Tc -0.3026 Tw T*
(when two or more nodes begin transmitting frames, or In-Frame Response d\ata, simultaneously.)Tj
/T1_0 9.75 Tf
0.2325 Tc 0 Tw -27 -24 Td
(3.3)Tj
0.1291 Tc -0.0896 Tw 27 0 Td
(Class A Data Communications\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.105 Tc 2.9595 Tw 155.25 0 Td
(A system whereby vehicle wiring is reduced by the transmission and)Tj
0.1172 Tc 0.1254 Tw -155.25 -12 Td
(reception of multiple signals over the same signal bus between nodes tha\t would have been accomplished by)Tj
0.1078 Tc 1.4317 Tw T*
(individual wires in a conventionally wired vehicle.  The nodes used to a\ccomplish multiplexed body wiring)Tj
0.1117 Tc -0.0365 Tw T*
(typically did not exist in the same or similar form in a conventionally \wired vehicle.)Tj
/T1_0 9.75 Tf
0.2325 Tc 0 Tw -27 -24 Td
(3.4)Tj
0.1291 Tc -0.0896 Tw 27 0 Td
(Class B Data Communications\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1199 Tc 3.5863 Tw 155.25 0 Td
(A system whereby data \(e.g., parametric data values\) is transferred)Tj
0.1399 Tc 1.6496 Tw -155.25 -12 Td
(between nodes to eliminate redundant sensors and other system elements. \ The nodes in this form of a)Tj
0.1188 Tc -0.2512 Tw T*
(multiplex system typically already existed as stand-alone modules in a c\onventionally wired vehicle.  A Class B)Tj
0.1296 Tc -0.2567 Tw T*
(network shall also be capable of performing Class A functions.)Tj
/T1_0 9.75 Tf
0.2325 Tc 0 Tw -27 -24 Td
