(An unbiased network is all conductors at ground voltage and the impedanc\e of the)Tj
0.1358 Tc 0.3412 Tw -91.5 -12 Td
(conductors not controlled.  No communication is possible on an unbiased \network.  The media must first)Tj
0.1136 Tc 0.6171 Tw 0 -12 TD
(be brought to the biased state before communication can take place.  The\ transition of the network from)Tj
0.098 Tc 0.6498 Tw T*
(the unbiased to the biased state may serve as a node wake-up signal for \certain applications, but this is)Tj
0.1103 Tc 0.1792 Tw T*
(not a requirement \(i.e., it is possible for individual nodes to be in t\he sleep state on a fully biased network)Tj
0.1457 Tc -0.325 Tw T*
(or in the awake state on an unbiased network\).)Tj
/T1_2 9.75 Tf
0.1335 Tc 0 Tw -45 -24 Td
(8.8.1.2)Tj
0.1386 Tc 0.1509 Tw 45 0 Td
(Biased Network\227)Tj
