0.1096 Tc -0.0508 Tw (A biased network is all conductors at the \223passive\224 voltage level \\(with no communication)Tj
0.0998 Tc 0.9397 Tw T*
(occurring\) and with appropriate impedances capable of supporting commun\ication.  Individual nodes on)Tj
0.0879 Tc 1.3069 Tw T*
(the network may exist in any of the three states described as follows.  \Note that nodes which use the)Tj
0.1061 Tc 0.0896 Tw T*
(optional sleep state are required to wake up from the appropriate networ\k signal within a defined wake-up)Tj
0.1106 Tc 2.2525 Tw T*
(period.  In other words, all nodes which are capable of wake-up from net\work signals must do so;)Tj
0.1246 Tc -0.2851 Tw T*
(otherwise these nodes are considered \223unpowered.\224  This requiremen\t assures a finite and limited delay to)Tj
-0.0601 Tw T*
(establish communication with nodes which may be in the sleep state.)Tj
0.119 Tc -0.0664 Tw 0 -24 TD
(The time required for the media to make the transition from the unbiased\ to the biased state is not defined)Tj
0.1391 Tc 0.5254 Tw 0 -12 TD
(in this document, since this parameter is largely application dependent \and, in fact, may not even occur)Tj
0.1092 Tc 1.0136 Tw T*
(\(e.g., media always biased\).  For the same reason, the time required f\or a node to make the transition)Tj
0.1243 Tc -0.0656 Tw T*
(between the unpowered state and the sleep or awake state is also not def\ined.)Tj
