(\227)Tj
0.0988 Tc 2.1407 Tw (The bit-by-bit arbitration scheme described as follows settles the confl\icts that)Tj
0.1043 Tc 1.6852 Tw -102.75 -12 Td
(occur when multiple nodes attempt to transmit frames simultaneously.  Th\is scheme is applied to each)Tj
0.1037 Tc 0.7691 Tw 0 -12 TD
(symbol/bit of the frame, starting with the SOF symbol and continuing unt\il the end of the frame.  Bit-by-bit)Tj
0.1173 Tc 0.0651 Tw T*
(arbitration is based on the use, at the physical layer, of two values of\ the bus called the active state and the)Tj
0.1103 Tc 0.2582 Tw T*
(passive state.  All symbols and bits are encoded on the bus by the physi\cal layer as combinations of active)Tj
0.0811 Tc 0.7584 Tw T*
(and passive state signals.  During simultaneous transmissions of active \state and passive state signals on)Tj
0.0994 Tc 1.0235 Tw T*
(the bus, the resultant state on the bus is always active \(active state \dominates\).  If the transmitting node)Tj
0.1018 Tc 1.0167 Tw T*
(detects a signal state on the bus that is different from the state being\ transmitted by the node during the)Tj
0.0927 Tc -0.1189 Tw T*
(header portion of the frame, the node must discontinue the transmit oper\ation prior to the start of the next bit.)Tj
0.1026 Tc 0.1869 Tw T*
(If the transmitting node detects a signal state on the bus that is diffe\rent from the state being transmitted by)Tj
0.0825 Tc 0.0746 Tw T*
(the node during the data portion of the frame \(following the header\), \the process used to cease transmission)Tj
0.1026 Tc 0.0797 Tw T*
(is implementation specific.  Some possible options are:)Tj
-0.3158 Tc 0 Tw 9 -24 Td
(a.)Tj
0.0662 Tc 2.2968 Tw 18 0 Td
(Discontinue the transmit operation prior to the start of the next bit \(\similar to the action taken if)Tj
0.1114 Tc 2.6424 Tw T*
(contention is detected during the header phase\).  If transmission of a \message is prematurely)Tj
0.1158 Tc 1.443 Tw T*
(terminated on a byte boundary due to unexpected contention detection fol\lowing the header, care)Tj
0.1097 Tc 1.1798 Tw T*
(must be taken by receiving nodes not to accept the message as a valid on\e.  There is a 1 in 256)Tj
0.0906 Tc -0.1169 Tw T*
(chance that the last byte received is the CRC of the previous bytes and \would therefore appear to be a)Tj
0.1038 Tc 0.2607 Tw T*
(valid message.  In this case, a node may need to validate the received m\essage to ensure it is of the)Tj
0.0132 Tc 0.2763 Tw T*
(correct length.)Tj
-0.3158 Tc 0 Tw -18 -12 Td
(b.)Tj
0.1465 Tc 0.9399 Tw 18 0 Td
(Transmit additional bits \(<8\) when contention is detected on a byte bo\undary.  This ensures that a)Tj
0.1066 Tc 1.1329 Tw T*
(framing error will be received by all other receivers in the case of une\xpected contention detection)Tj
0.0724 Tc -0.0329 Tw T*
(possibly due to noise.)Tj
0.1127 Tc 0.7504 Tw -27 -20.25 Td
(Bus access is granted to nodes sending an active state signal over nodes\ sending a passive state signal.)Tj
0.13 Tc 0.3801 Tw T*
(Figure 21 shows this operation on the physical layer, based on the two f\orms of modulation allowed \(PWM)Tj
-0.0226 Tc 0.3121 Tw T*
(and VPW\).)Tj
0.1313 Tc 0 Tw 0 -24 TD
(The arbitration process begins with the SOF and continues through all th\e bits of the frames being sent.  As)Tj
0.1179 Tc -0.3416 Tw 0 -12 TD
(each symbol or bit of all the simultaneous frames is transmitted, all of\ the nodes still transmitting after the last)Tj
0.1205 Tc 1.3602 Tw T*
(symbol or bit will detect whether any contention is taking place.  Nodes\ that detect contention have, by)Tj
0.1235 Tc 0.0254 Tw T*
(definition, lost arbitration and will discontinue sending any further sy\mbols or bits.  Any remaining nodes will)Tj
0.1206 Tc -0.3605 Tw T*
(continue to send their symbols/bits until the next contention is detecte\d.  The node which obtains sole access)Tj
0.0892 Tc 0.1467 Tw T*
(to the medium is that which sends its symbols and bits without detecting\ any contention.)Tj
0.1632 Tc 0 Tw -36 -24 Td
