(Start of Frame \(SOF\)\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1192 Tc 1.0609 Tw 103.5 0 Td
(The SOF mark is used to uniquely identify the start of a frame.  The SOF\ mark)Tj
0.0908 Tc 0.0112 Tw -103.5 -12 Td
(shall not be used in the calculation of the CRC error detection code.)Tj
/T1_2 9.75 Tf
0.1335 Tc 0 Tw -45 -24 Td
(7.3.4.2)Tj
0.1373 Tc 0.1522 Tw 45 0 Td
(End of Data \(EOD\)\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1338 Tc 0.9057 Tw 93.75 0 Td
(End of Data \(EOD\) is used to signal the end of transmission by the ori\ginator of a)Tj
0.1081 Tc -0.0269 Tw -93.75 -12 Td
(frame. The in-frame response \(IFR\) section of the frame, if used, begi\ns after the EOD time but before the)Tj
0.1193 Tc 0.8412 Tw T*
(EOF. If the IFR feature \(see 7.3.7\) is not used, then the bus would re\main in the passive state thereby)Tj
0.0999 Tc 0.1896 Tw T*
(resulting in an End of Frame \(EOF\).  If a frame includes an IFR, the o\riginator of the frame will expect the)Tj
0.1202 Tc 1.8693 Tw T*
(recipient\(s\) of the frame to drive the network with one or more in-fra\me response bytes immediately)Tj
0.0949 Tc -0.5554 Tw T*
(following EOD.)Tj
/T1_2 9.75 Tf
0.1335 Tc 0 Tw -45 -24 Td
(7.3.4.3)Tj
0.051 Tc 0.2385 Tw 45 0 Td
(End of Frame \(EOF\)\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.0875 Tc 0.6841 Tw 100.5 0 Td
(The completion of the EOF defines the end of a frame. After the last tra\nsmission)Tj
0.0996 Tc 0.7634 Tw -100.5 -12 Td
(byte \(including in-frame response bytes where applicable\), the bus wil\l be left in a passive state.  When)Tj
0.0822 Tc 0.124 Tw T*
(EOF has expired, all receivers will consider the transmission complete.)Tj
/T1_2 9.75 Tf
0.1335 Tc 0 Tw -45 -24 Td
(7.3.4.4)Tj
0.1485 Tc -0.234 Tw 45 0 Td
(Inter-Frame Separation \(IFS\)\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1358 Tc 0.3204 Tw 138 0 Td
(Inter-Frame Separation is used to allow proper synchronization of variou\s)Tj
0.0963 Tc 0.8896 Tw -138 -12 Td
(nodes during back-to-back frame transmissions.  A transmitter must not i\nitiate transmission on the bus)Tj
0.151 Tc -0.2834 Tw T*
(before the completion of the IFS minimum period.  However, receivers mus\t synchronize to any other SOF)Tj
0.1004 Tc 0.0016 Tw T*
(occurring after the EOF minimum period in order to accommodate individua\l clock tolerances.)Tj
