0.1155 Tc 1.1383 Tw (Although various methods of data bus control can be used, this Class B n\etwork is)Tj
0.1283 Tc 0.3956 Tw -82.5 -12 Td
(intended for \223masterless\224 bus control.  The principal advantage of\ the masterless bus control concept is its)Tj
0.1116 Tc 0.2716 Tw T*
(ability to provide the basis for an open-architecture data communication\s system.  Since a master does not)Tj
0.0657 Tc 0.0155 Tw T*
(exist, each node has an equal opportunity to initiate a data transmissio\n once an idle bus has been detected.)Tj
0.1059 Tc 1.6836 Tw T*
(However, not all nodes and/or data are of equal importance, prioritizati\on of frames is allowed and the)Tj
0.089 Tc -0.0201 Tw T*
(highest priority frame will always be completed.  This also implies that\ frame/data contention will not result in)Tj
0.1244 Tc 0.6807 Tw T*
(lost data.  Two disadvantages of the masterless bus concept are that dat\a latency cannot be guaranteed,)Tj
0.1408 Tc -0.2513 Tw T*
(except for the single highest system priority frame, and bus utilization\ extremes are difficult to evaluate.)Tj
/T1_0 9.75 Tf
0.2325 Tc 0 Tw -36 -24 Td
