-0.3158 Tc -255 674.25 Td
(1.)Tj
0.2484 Tc 27 0 Td
(Scope\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.0873 Tc 3.0772 Tw 39.75 0 Td
(This SAE Standard establishes the requirements for a Class B Data Commun\ication Network)Tj
0.1134 Tc 2.8011 Tw -39.75 -12 Td
(Interface applicable to all On- and Off-Road Land-Based Vehicles.  It de\fines a minimum set of data)Tj
0.0922 Tc 2.1588 Tw 0 -12 TD
(communication requirements such that the resulting network is cost effec\tive for simple applications and)Tj
0.1016 Tc 0.7504 Tw T*
(flexible enough to use in complex applications.  Taken in total, the req\uirements contained in this document)Tj
0.0876 Tc 0.2019 Tw T*
(specify a data communications network that satisfies the needs of automo\tive manufacturers.)Tj
0.1257 Tc 1.7888 Tw 0 -24 TD
(This specification describes two specific implementations of the network\, based on media/Physical Layer)Tj
0.1082 Tc 0.8919 Tw 0 -12 TD
(differences.  One Physical Layer is optimized for a data rate of 10.4 Kb\ps while the other Physical Layer is)Tj
0.1072 Tc 0.6823 Tw T*
(optimized for a data rate of 41.6 Kbps \(see Appendix A for a checklist \of application-specific features\).  The)Tj
0.1516 Tc 1.2161 Tw T*
(Physical Layer parameters are specified as they would be detected on the\ network media, not within any)Tj
0.0878 Tc 0.0517 Tw T*
(particular module or integrated circuit implementation.)Tj
0.0969 Tc 3.1457 Tw 0 -24 TD
(Although devices may be constructed that can be configured to operate in\ either of the two primary)Tj
0.0927 Tc -0.1032 Tw 0 -12 TD
(implementations defined herein, it is expected that most manufacturers w\ill focus specifically on either the 10.4)Tj
0.1061 Tc 0.7027 Tw T*
(Kbps implementation or the 41.6 Kbps implementation depending on their s\pecific application and corporate)Tj
0.1146 Tc 0.521 Tw T*
(philosophy toward network usage.  However, low-volume users of network-i\nterface devices are expected to)Tj
0.0998 Tc 1.5491 Tw T*
(find it more effective to use a generic interface capable of handling ei\ther of the primary implementations)Tj
0.0832 Tc 0.2063 Tw T*
(specified in this document.)Tj
0.1098 Tc 0.5547 Tw 0 -24 TD
(This SAE document is under the control and maintenance of the Vehicle Ne\tworks for Multiplexing and Data)Tj
0.0984 Tc 0.3065 Tw 0 -12 TD
(Communications \(Multiplex\) Committee.  This committee will periodicall\y review and update this document as)Tj
0.039 Tc 0.2505 Tw T*
(needs dictate.)Tj
/T1_0 9.75 Tf
0.2325 Tc 0 Tw -27 -24 Td
(1.1)Tj
0.085 Tc 27 0 Td
(Objectives\227)Tj
/T1_1 9.75 Tf
0.1264 Tc 0.1631 Tw 60.75 0 Td
(This document constitutes the requirements for a vehicle-data communicat\ions network.  These)Tj
0.1246 Tc -0.0998 Tw -60.75 -12 Td
(requirements are related to the lowest two layers of the ISO Open System\ Interconnect \(OSI\) model \(Ref. ISO)Tj
0.1026 Tc 0.1474 Tw T*
(7498\).  These layers are the Data Link Layer and the Physical Layer.  T\his network has been described using)Tj
0.1327 Tc -0.0197 Tw T*
(the ISO conventions in ISO/TC 22/SC 3/WG1 N429 E, dated October, 1990.  \Both documents are intended to)Tj
0.0984 Tc 0.0411 Tw T*
(describe the same network requirements but using different descriptive s\tyles.  If any technical differences are)Tj
0.0873 Tc 0.0522 Tw T*
(identified, the very latest revision of these documents should be used.)Tj
0.1111 Tc 1.6316 Tw 0 -24 TD
(This document has been submitted as an American National Standard.  As s\uch, its format is somewhat)Tj
0.1362 Tc 1.2562 Tw 0 -12 TD
(different from the formal ISO description in that descriptions have been\ expanded, but are in no way less)Tj
0.1281 Tc -0.1886 Tw T*
(precise.  A more textual format has been adopted herein to allow explana\tions to be included.)Tj
0.1328 Tc 1.2067 Tw 0 -24 TD
(The vehicle application for this class of data communication \(Class B\)\ network is defined \(Reference SAE)Tj
0.1261 Tc 1.2663 Tw 0 -12 TD
(J1213 APR88\) to allow the sharing of vehicle parametric information.  A\lso per the definition, this Class B)Tj
0.1071 Tc -0.0988 Tw T*
(network shall be capable of performing Class A functions.)Tj
/T1_2 9.75 Tf
